From e1ba92f0530543c073d00429da2c6bf14e40132e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:29:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: skip pack files identical to a baseline pack and unused
 OptiFine sky images

Add the baseline_pack_path global option (PackSquash #402). Pack files that
are identical to the file with the same path in a baseline pack, a directory
or a ZIP such as a vanilla client JAR, are left out of the result ZIP.
Textures are compared by pixels, JSON by contents, other files byte by byte,
and a texture is only left out together with its animation metadata.

Add the skip_unused_optifine_sky_images global option, which leaves out
OptiFine custom sky images that no sky entry names.

Add PackFileStatus::intentionally_skipped so the CLI does not warn about
files that the options ask to leave out.
